# Tooltips

Use [Material tooltips](https://squidfunk.github.io/mkdocs-material/reference/tooltips/) for a link title or an abbreviation. `abbr`, `attr_list`, `pymdownx.snippets`, and `content.tooltips` are enabled. Do not add a glossary file.

Spell a term out in the sentence the first time it appears. A tooltip is easy to miss, and it is unavailable to someone who does not hover.

```markdown
[table of contents](summaries/index.md "The summary block")
```

- Put the title in quotes after the URL, inside the same parentheses. There is one space before the quotes.
- The title is a short phrase, not a sentence of instructions.
- An abbreviation is `*[PDF]: Portable Document Format`, placed anywhere in the file. Every later `PDF` on that page gets the tooltip.
- Do not gather abbreviations into `includes/abbreviations.md`.
